[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441882698","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/112#issuecomment-441882698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/112","id":441882698,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTg4MjY5OA==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-03-25T14:06:35Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T03:08:36Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\n> Consider two migrations: A and B; A succeeds while B fails due to some error. After database migration you get A fully applied and B partially applied or not applied at all.\n\nthis is because your database doesn't support [transactional ddl](http://wiki.postgresql.org/wiki/Transactional_DDL_in_PostgreSQL:_A_Competitive_Analysis).\n\n> However, the migrations table remains empty. Once I fix B I should be able to rerun just B but A is executed as well.\n\nalembic does do this for when transactional DDL isn't on, on line 212 of migrations.py:\n\n            change(**kw)\n            if not self.impl.transactional_ddl:\n                self._update_current_rev(prev_rev, rev)\n            prev_rev = rev\n\nso then I checked what env.py does, by default it's this:\n\n    try:\n        with context.begin_transaction():\n            context.run_migrations()\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\n\nso that's the problem right?  wrong, begin_transaction() *also* checks transactional DDL, and doesn't actually run a transaction:\n\n    def begin_transaction(self):\n        if not self.is_transactional_ddl():\n            @contextmanager\n            def do_nothing():\n                yield\n            return do_nothing()\n        elif self.is_offline_mode():\n            @contextmanager\n            def begin_commit():\n                self.get_context().impl.emit_begin()\n                yield\n                self.get_context().impl.emit_commit()\n            return begin_commit()\n        else:\n            return self.get_bind().begin()\n\n\nso I am not seeing how your error is occurring, unless your tranasctional_ddl flag is  incorrectly set.   The version table is written after each migration and the connection is in autocommit mode when transactional_ddl is false.  I need a lot more detail here including database in use as well as some log output.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/comments/441882698/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.gi